.TH BUILDABOOK 1 "October 2026" "buildabook 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
buildabook \- build a typeset book from a plain-text outline
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buildabook
.RI [ typst | pdf | cover | check | number-map | uuid ]
.RI [ options ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buildabook
turns a plain-text outline into a typeset book.  One outline file drives the
chapter numbering, the table of contents, and every cross-reference, so the
book is a build artifact of a single source of order.
.PP
The program reads
.IR outline.txt ,
the one source of sequence and numbering, resolves
.B {{token}}
cross-references in the chapter source files, and writes a Typst
.I book.typ
together with a
.I number_map.csv
audit.
.PP
The point of the tool is that a writer, human or LLM, never writes a number or
a page reference by hand.  The prose holds stable tokens such as
.BR {{c:id00042}} ;
buildabook computes the number at build time from the outline's row order, and
page references resolve through native Typst lookups.  Inserting, deleting, or
reordering a chapter is one line in the outline; every reference follows on
the next build.  The
.B check
subcommand catches the mistakes a prose pass cannot hold in its head, such as
duplicate UUIDs, unmatched files, and unresolvable tokens.
.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
With no subcommand,
.B buildabook
builds all three stages in order, building whatever it can: a missing or
failing stage is reported and the next stage is still attempted when its own
inputs are present.
.TP
.B typst
Render the book: parse the outline, resolve tokens, and emit
.IR rendered/book.typ
plus
.IR number_map.csv .
.TP
.B pdf
Compile
.IR rendered/book.typ
to the book PDF with Typst.
.TP
.B cover
Update the cover spine width from the book PDF's page count (via
.BR pdfinfo (1)),
then compile the cover with Typst.  Skipped with a warning when there is no
cover source or no book PDF.
.TP
.B check
Validate the outline, the file map, and every token reference.  Emit nothing;
exit nonzero on the first error.
.TP
.B number-map
Write
.I number_map.csv
only.
.TP
.BR uuid " [" c | p | a | d | n | s | k ]
Print the next free UUID (the highest
.B idNNNNN
already in use, in the outline and the source files, plus one).  An optional
prefix prints it as
.IR prefix :idNNNNN ,
for a writer minting a fresh chapter, section, or anchor reference.
.
.SH OPTIONS
A command-line flag overrides
.IR book.conf ,
which overrides the built-in default.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Book config to read (default
.IR book.conf ,
if present).
.TP
.BI \-\-outline " file"
Outline file (default
.IR outline.txt ).
.TP
.BI \-\-src " dir"
Directory holding the chapter source files (default
.IR chapters ).
.TP
.BI \-\-out " dir"
Directory for the rendered output (default
.IR rendered ).
.TP
.BI \-\-filemap " file"
Authoritative
.IR UUID:filename
map (default
.IR filemap.txt ,
if present; otherwise headings are matched).
.TP
.BI \-\-template " file"
Typst template to emit from (default
.IR book.header.typ ,
else
.IR book.prefix.typ ,
else the shared
.IR template/book.typ ).
.TP
.BI \-\-number-map " file"
Where to write the CSV audit (default
.IR number_map.csv ).
.TP
.BI \-\-slug " name"
Book slug used to derive output names (default: the directory name).
.TP
.BI \-\-pdf " file"
Book PDF output (default
.IR <slug> .pdf).
.TP
.BI \-\-cover-src " file"
Cover source (default
.IR cover.typ ).
.TP
.BI \-\-cover " file"
Cover PDF output (default
.IR <slug> -cover.pdf).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I outline.txt
The outline: one entry or directive per line, with
.B #
comments.  See
.BR LANGUAGE.md .
.TP
.I filemap.txt
Optional
.IR UUID:filename
map.  When absent, each source file is matched by its first heading.
.TP
.I book.conf
Book metadata and build paths in the OpenBSD-style configuration language,
parsed by the hbnf runtime.  See
.B "CONFIGURATION"
below.
.TP
.I template/book.typ
The shared default Typst template.
.TP
.I number_map.csv
Generated audit of every UUID and its rendered designation.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I book.conf
is obconf syntax: bareword or "quoted" directives, `{ }` blocks, `#`
comments, `;`- or newline-terminated entries.
.PP
.nf
title "Telegraph to Turbo Jet"
author "David Walther"
slug   speedrun-telegraph-to-turbo-jet

build {
    outline    outline.txt
    src        chapters
    out        rendered
    template   book.header.typ
    number-map number_map.csv
}

cover {
    source cover.typ
    output speedrun-cover.pdf
}
.fi
.PP
Every field is optional; a field left out falls back to the built-in default
(and any
.B \-\-
flag still overrides).  A malformed file is reported as
.I file:line:col: message
and stops the run.
.
.SH LIMITATIONS
.PP
A title or directive value runs to end of line, so it cannot contain a literal
newline, and there is no trailing-comment syntax.  Each entry is addressed by a
UUID written
.BR idNNNNN ,
which is a name, not a number; the writer must look up a UUID rather than a
number, and
.I number_map.csv
is the look-up aid.  A page reference to a section requires that section's
heading to carry its token.  A
.B k:
sub-entry binds to the chapter whose UUID is its
.B NNNNN
part, which the engine does not verify at parse time.  The book is emitted as
one Typst document; splitting a book across volumes is a Makefile-level
concern, not an engine feature.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; nonzero if the outline, file map, the config, or a token
reference is invalid, or if a subcommand is unknown.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
buildabook                    # typst -> pdf -> cover, building what it can
buildabook check
buildabook typst --outline outline.txt --src chapters --out rendered
buildabook cover --cover speedrun-cover.pdf
buildabook number-map
.fi
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR LANGUAGE.md ,
.BR typst (1)
.
